Package: dev.diffterm.app
Name: diffTerm
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: @ARCH@
Maintainer: andi <tafilajandi@gmail.com>
Author: andi
Section: Terminal_Support
Priority: optional
Depends: firmware (>= 14.0)
Icon: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/@REPO@/main/assets/icon.png
Native-Depiction: https://@PAGES@/depiction.json
SileoDepiction: https://@PAGES@/depiction.json
Tag: role::hacker
Description: A different terminal to use
 A real shell on your jailbroken iPhone or iPad, drawn the way a terminal is
 supposed to be.
 .
 The emulator is written from scratch against the DEC VT500 state diagram:
 VT100/VT220/xterm controls, 24-bit colour, the alternate screen, scroll
 regions, mouse reporting, Sixel and iTerm2 inline images. Conformance is
 measured with esctest rather than claimed.
 .
 Shells run inside the app and end with it. When iOS reclaims diffTerm in
 the background, each tab's screen is saved and comes back on relaunch,
 marked so old output is not mistaken for a live shell.
 .
 OSC 133 shell integration marks every command, so you can jump between
 prompts, copy one command's output, and see exit codes and run times.
 Autosuggestions and command completion cover 700+ tools.
